{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791142621,"nonce":"2kG5Pk6paUDXRcGH+39ktUQ2MsI=","title":"A burst of garbage before an idle period is held until something allocates again","message":"Reported by ashui-8b: ashui's ChartsGallery, AOT (no JIT), RSS once a second:\n132MB at 1s, 301 at 2s, 319 at 3-9s, 192MB from 10s on, under 1% CPU. About ten\ncharts run a 0.6s entrance animation that rebuilds paths/contours per frame: a\nsecond of short-lived allocation, all garbage once it ends. The heap holds it\n~6s until a collection happens to run. Hybrid peaks at 410MB and settles at 234.\n\nWhy: the trigger is allocation-driven only. threshold = live * growth\n(growth 4x, adapting up to 16x), clamped to [8MB, ceiling], ceiling =\nusable RAM / 32 clamped to [64MB, 512MB] -- 512MB on a 16GB Mac. A burst under\nthe threshold followed by idle never reaches it, and the 30s HEARTBEAT also\nfires only on an allocation.\n\nUI programs allocate in bursts (startup, entrances, scrolling) with idle time\nafter. Candidate: collect when the mutator goes idle with a large\nbytes_since_gc -- e.g. at hl_blocking(true) or the event loop's wait, if\nbytes_since_gc exceeds a fraction of the threshold and some minimum -- and/or a\nheartbeat that does not wait for an allocation.","files":null}]}